    ],
    "note": "Staging output for Batch 2.4 (mk-designsystem tokens, D-317). Each of the 5 theme objects below (hibr/kufi/naqsh/raml/tayf) mirrors the MKTheme Swift protocol shape 1:1: colors, fonts, typeRamp, spacing, radii, elevation, motion. Colors are packed #RRGGBB hex, matching Color(hex:) in MKThemeColorHelpers.swift; a {ref: <role>} value means the Swift property is a computed passthrough to another semantic role on the SAME theme (e.g. Kufi secondary returns primary), not an independent color -- resolve within the same theme object. primaryPressed values are computed via Color.darkened(hex:, by: 0.12) = each RGB channel * 0.88 rounded to nearest int; there is no literal Swift hex constant for these, they are recomputed here to the same precision. spacing and motion are byte-identical across all 5 themes because every Swift theme conformer's `spacing`/`motion` property resolves to `.default` (MKSpacing.default / MKMotionTokens.default) -- duplicated per theme here intentionally so Batch 2.4 can consume one theme object without cross-referencing another. typeRamp role sizes (pointSize/lineHeightMultiplier/weight) are also theme-independent per MKTypeRamp.swift; only the resolved `face` (font PostScript name) differs per theme, via fonts.<faceRole>.",
    "themeIdOrder": [
      "hibr",
      "kufi",
      "naqsh",
      "raml",
      "tayf"
    ]
  },
